Figure 3: $E_{\rm peak}-\beta$ parameter space (so-called $\beta$-plot) built from the LogParabola parametrization of Eq. (2) for AGNs (blue), pulsars (red) – illustrated by filled contours, marking their one, two and three-sigma outline – and DM (purple). The latter region is obtained by fitting a DM annihilation spectrum for all possible two-channel combinations, for DM masses from $5$ GeV to 100 TeV.
The two unID subsamples defined in our study are also shown in these plots;
see Section 3.2 for details. Left: In green, the 220 unIDs belonging to Subsample I. The rest of the 445 unIDs that survived our initial selection cuts in Section 3.1 are depicted in gray. Right: A zoomed-in region of the $\beta$-plot is shown, with the unIDs of Subsample II highlighted in orange. Now, gray points refer to those unIDs in Subsample I that were excluded after our multi-wavelength analysis.

